<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:14Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump envoys, European officials to discuss ‘new ideas’ for Ukraine peace in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:235629fa7c9cf55c390c579e0f3d8b05e7d14947cf0fed9798ca60acadad3056</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T21:19:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami--619d0e85a342.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-trump-envoys-ukraine-peace-talks-miami" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump’s envoys will meet Ukrainian negotiators and European officials in Miami on Friday to discuss new proposals to end Russia’s war in Ukraine, two US sources told AFP. Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will present ideas developed during recent talks with both sides, one source said Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Black sea and black ops: How exposed is Europe to Ukraine war spillover?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:536a2d2f0bfcede0c29dd883b567164ea9ee3807300d22417928e113e3bf0f24</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:42:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover--b0bb3b79e51f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261008-black-sea-and-black-ops-how-exposed-is-europe-to-ukraine-war-spillover" /><summary type="html">The story’s as underreported as it is consequential for the entire planet: Three Turkish-owned cargo ships out of Ukraine hit in EU waters by suspected Russian drones. One, the Togo-flagged Alfa Watan sinking Tuesday off Bulgaria. Ten Egyptian and Syrian crew missing. For its part, Ukraine’s been hitting Russian tankers in the Black Sea... this with no sign of a return to a UN-brokered deal to allow oil, grain and fertilizer ships to pass.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Spain mourns Maricarmen Abascal, whose eviction sparked housing protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:051ded19fafdb57fadad1f3e8ddda60b751105502ca9e526a7596a682519498a</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests--91508a8d7343.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-mourns-maricarmen-abascal-whose-eviction-sparked-housing-protests" /><summary type="html">Protests and anger have grown across Spain after the death of an 87-year-old woman in the wake of her eviction from her home. Maricarmen Abascal was thrown out of her home of seven decades in what became the "cause celebre" of Spain's housing crisis. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Nothing will stop us’: French student protests show few signs of ending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a99486d979aa18afb98e16065be8e07f8a6a156466e2e9d09b5886982a225334</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:22:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261008-nothing-will-stop-us-french-student-protests-show-few-signs-of-ending--7c28dd5ef3a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261008-nothing-will-stop-us-french-student-protests-show-few-signs-of-ending" /><summary type="html">Students on Thursday barricaded a Parisian high school with garbage bins before police shot tear gas at them as France’s nationwide protests showed little sign of ending. At least a dozen demonstrations supporting the high school students’ movement were planned across the country while 375 schools were fully or partially closed.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>'Fighting for our future': France high school students vow no let-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18b5096ba8b5742bd2c5d85e2016ada790a1c7c0604b198ce92f68ee1702effd</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:17:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fighting-for-our-future-france-high-school-students-vow-no-let-up--cf14a45bec6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fighting-for-our-future-france-high-school-students-vow-no-let-up" /><summary type="html">Over 70,000 people took part in demonstrations across France on Thursday demanding better education and less police brutality, as students protested nationwide despite government attempts to ease a crisis that has rocked the country for more than a week. Students have blocked entrances to hundreds of high schools, with squads of riot police deployed  -- occasionally resulting in violent clashes. The interior ministry said 71,500 participated in protests across the country, with police detaining more than 500 people. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from central Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Aaron Sorkin, Mikey Madison, Jeremy Allen White: The director and cast behind the Facebook sequel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6b7fc041c7e9c85ba39bc6985b1f02862ad0caef2432b363cad8da4ff10b98d</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T17:42:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261008-aaron-sorkin-mikey-madison-jeremy-allen-white-the-director-and-cast-behind-the-facebook-seq--1fa7da6248b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261008-aaron-sorkin-mikey-madison-jeremy-allen-white-the-director-and-cast-behind-the-facebook-sequel" /><summary type="html">Fifteen years after "The Social Network", Aaron Sorkin is taking on Facebook again. His new film, "The Social Reckoning", looks at what the platform has become and the role it plays in division, extremism and misinformation in America, themes that have fuelled his long-running public feud with Mark Zuckerberg. It tells the true story of Facebook whistleblower Frances Haugen, played by Oscar-nominated actress Mikey Madison ("Anora"), who leaked thousands of internal documents to Wall Street Journal reporter Jeff Horwitz, played by Jeremy Allen White ("The Bear").</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian poet and essayist Anne Carson wins Nobel Prize in literature</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c046d7892f20d3cc0457f704cf69140c4e97e95e9aef5e864ade45198dc4ab6</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T17:12:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-canadian-poet-and-essayist-anne-carson-wins-nobel-prize-in-literature--0e062a53b413.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-canadian-poet-and-essayist-anne-carson-wins-nobel-prize-in-literature" /><summary type="html">Canadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson won the Nobel Prize in literature Thursday for playful, genre-blending works that fuse the classical and the modern. The Toronto-born Carson, 76, draws on themes and stories from ancient Greek and Roman literature for writing that often blends elements of poetry, essay and fiction.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian attack on Ukraine busses part of 'a steady increase in attacks on civilians'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6b2cd741e8d7f289c6b3896700e50b9b4fc57dac83ae0b5629115539e30b1b9</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T17:11:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-russian-attack-on-ukraine-busses-part-of-a-steady-increase-in-attacks-on-civilians--a9efafb20e09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-russian-attack-on-ukraine-busses-part-of-a-steady-increase-in-attacks-on-civilians" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Thursday there would be a response to a Russian strike that hit two buses in the frontline city of Kramatorsk, killing 30 people and wounding 18 others. France 24's Andrew Hilliar says it comes a bid a growing number of Russian attacks on civilians in the country, with UN figures showing that more civilians had been killed in Ukraine as of August this year than in all of 2025.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Russian-occupied town in Ukraine facing starvation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45a65c5e45c37d90bf3bb74951626c43a8284c75939122c59c2f0fd254922f00</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T17:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-the-russian-occupied-town-in-ukraine-facing-starvation--251767b71b20.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-the-russian-occupied-town-in-ukraine-facing-starvation" /><summary type="html">Trapped and facing starvation, residents of the Russian-occupied town of Oleshky in southern Ukraine risk their lives to travel for hours by foot and bicycle along mine-strewn roads to get food and water. The town near the Ukrainian city of Kherson on the war's southern front has been under Russian control since 2022. Since May, food deliveries have dried up, and now former residents and Ukrainian refugees are trying to sound the alarm.</summary></entry><entry><title>As elections near, how are French political parties reacting to student protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b43e511618fec08d485fb6d33435df6f9a379e3b905c05f7059e7a8dbe3125db</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T17:08:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-as-elections-near-how-are-french-political-parties-reacting-to-student-protests--a96b6e161ee8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-as-elections-near-how-are-french-political-parties-reacting-to-student-protests" /><summary type="html">Students in France are pledging to keep taking to the streets despite the country's prime minister making a speech on Wednesday in which he said the government would come up with a plan to address their concerns. How have political parties in France been reacting to the movement? Delano D'Souza has been finding out.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two Latvian men arrested at UK base housing US and NATO intelligence hubs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e41b3f9797e1829d97e45bd54be78966e41f0e189cf9be6a7e1fc1800c81517</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:57:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs--393dadf82f17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-two-latvian-men-arrested-at-uk-base-housing-us-and-nato-intelligence-hubs" /><summary type="html">British ​counter-terrorism police are investigating after two Latvian men were arrested Thursday near a Royal Air Force ​base in southeast England housing US and NATO intelligence operations, police said in a statement. The arrests come days after a major incident at another UK base led the US military to withdraw B-1 bombers stationed there.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French, US and Russian astronauts return to Earth after eight months in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ad737688c23c70af1f82725f7800edc2c18401d1abf6d1b10b8d7a8240337b3</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:02:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space--ded2d2b5229c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-french-us-and-russian-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space" /><summary type="html">SpaceX brought France's Sophie Adenot and fellow astronauts Jessica Meir, Jack Hathaway and Andrey Fedyaev back to Earth on Thursday after an eight-month mission on board the International Space Station that saw Adenot become the first French woman to walk in space.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>#IAmJaneDoe: A campaign in solidarity with Cornell alleged gang-rape victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e2d7abcd1395436a943cf10e5c259c51e795d1683bfc1f955e089de1a45467c</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:34:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-iamjanedoe-a-campaign-in-solidarity-with-cornell-alleged-gang-rape-victim--f34505628987.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-iamjanedoe-a-campaign-in-solidarity-with-cornell-alleged-gang-rape-victim" /><summary type="html">A wave of videos is spreading across social media under the hashtag #IAmJaneDoe to express solidarity with an anonymous Cornell University student who alleges she was sexually assaulted by several members of a fraternity in 2024.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘A celebration of the hybrid form’: Anne Carson wins Nobel literature prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69145dff311aa87d3931c5925a0c40cbff64f9a309a1c0e6b9b02ba77a2ebb42</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:30:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-a-celebration-of-the-hybrid-form-anne-carson-wins-nobel-literature-prize--814847bcf41e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-a-celebration-of-the-hybrid-form-anne-carson-wins-nobel-literature-prize" /><summary type="html">Canadian poet, essayist and translator Anne Carson won the Nobel Prize in literature Thursday for playful, genre-blending works that fuse the classical and the modern. Artist, podcast host and writer Mia Funk joined France 24 to discuss Carson’s work.</summary></entry><entry><title>Student protesters 'showing no signs of backing down'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fe1cdbce9d6b71dfedd567ecec59f790f07b9c54c29e1a1daf4ad2a7a0e557b</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:23:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-student-protesters-showing-no-signs-of-backing-down--2da2d207a7b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-student-protesters-showing-no-signs-of-backing-down" /><summary type="html">Students who have been protesting classroom conditions in France for days are "not looking like they are willing to back down", says France 24 reporter Claire Paccalin, despite promises by the French prime minister to bring in measures to address their grievances.</summary></entry><entry><title>How long will the global energy crunch last?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6cc2c2d13931f0c5ee2d75bd8d7d812ebf8d3a60451fed03891e0d70fa02875</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:05:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261008-how-long-will-the-global-energy-crunch-last--1d78a0acf96e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261008-how-long-will-the-global-energy-crunch-last" /><summary type="html">High energy prices continue to drive inflation and stoke anger among voters around the world. But with more crude oil flowing through the Strait of Hormuz, and governments releasing more emergency fuel stockpiles, how long will the energy crunch last?</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry><entry><title>Search warrants for former prince Andrew's homes were unlawful, UK court rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b61d1ec14d0eb85dc83177282da2ff475cb392eb03645ae2b40986ef33161375</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:09:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules--df9bf5d6c48d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261008-search-warrants-for-former-prince-andrew-homes-were-unlawful-uk-court-rules" /><summary type="html">Police who searched the properties of Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor as part of investigations into his links to the late sex offender Jeffrey Epstein have agreed the search warrants were unlawful, a London judge said Thursday. The 66-year-old younger brother of King Charles II was arrested on February 19 on suspicion of misconduct in public office.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Protest culture: Why do French students repeatedly rise up?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abbdaf734e64c006472f42905a015d5ecb648197ab2f74eed4bf91b958cd8fce</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:00:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261008-protest-culture-why-do-french-students-repeatedly-rise-up--076acebec9c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20261008-protest-culture-why-do-french-students-repeatedly-rise-up" /><summary type="html">France is in the international spotlight as massive student protests show no sign of stopping. Demonstrating is something of a rite of passage for young people in France, a moment when teenagers discover politics and their collective voice. How has this "protest culture" manifested itself in recent French history? And why are some student protests effective at bringing about change and others not? We take a closer look in French Connections.</summary><category term="French connections" /></entry><entry><title>Microsoft brings more AI to PCs as it challenges Apple</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f18434d3051f796ea781e10b738593a84521b9d8bbe2dd8bbb5d3cd792e1f21</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:25:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:45:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-microsoft-brings-more-ai-to-pcs-as-it-challenges-apple--25f4e8ede04a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-microsoft-brings-more-ai-to-pcs-as-it-challenges-apple" /><summary type="html">Microsoft unveiled on Wednesday an AI coding model that can run directly on personal computers and new security technology to prevent AI agents from accessing data without permission, challenging Apple's push to bring more AI into personal devices.</summary></entry><entry><title>30 dead in strike on Ukraine bus as Russian attacks intensify</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a1db1263a5d8f4e7efa63c2325373252d5c51a9d6e11deb41be1dcb3b4c9d07</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:44:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-30-dead-in-strike-on-ukraine-bus-as-russian-attacks-intensify--e17e35922460.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-30-dead-in-strike-on-ukraine-bus-as-russian-attacks-intensify" /><summary type="html">Thirty people were killed and at least 18 were injured by Russian strikes in eastern Ukraine that included an attack on a public bus, authorities said Thursday, as an intensive pre-winter wave of attacks continued.</summary></entry><entry><title>'They killed her': Evicted pensioner who sparked Spain housing protests dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35a4d24b5eb9df0707bbbabec22b14dac7ac3751d1fbe19c928aedba690e20bc</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:43:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-they-killed-her-evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies--1241c9662382.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-they-killed-her-evicted-pensioner-who-sparked-spain-housing-protests-dies" /><summary type="html">The 87-year-old whose eviction last month sparked nationwide protests in Spain has died. Maricarmen Abascal was evicted from her home of more than 70 years last month, after it was bought by an investment fund. After news of her passing, some who took to the streets say they believe her death was brought on by the stress of the eviction.</summary></entry><entry><title>High school student protests continue in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84b546ce6c4e61b57c87d011a05bf001d5ba6a3a7981820835e9eb721074fd13</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:40:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-high-school-student-protests-continue-in-france--0bc08479fcd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-high-school-student-protests-continue-in-france" /><summary type="html">#France: high school students continue to protest Thursday in the face of what they say is the government’s failure to respond to their demands. 
 
Follow the fourth day of protests on FRANCE 24</summary></entry><entry><title>New Paris exhibition explores Ireland's housing crisis through contemporary art</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69c08c4f2432473cb2de02d5efdf3a11d02a4ebf8366d10e972750896bedea97</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:29:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art--34e2c2f9b707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261008-new-paris-exhibition-explores-ireland-s-housing-crisis-through-contemporary-art" /><summary type="html">Huge demonstrations have been held over the last few weeks in Spain over its housing crisis, but the issue is not restricted to Spain. Many other countries also have a huge problem with housing, including Ireland, with experts saying that for every street of 10 houses, the country actually needs 12. Now a new exhibition in Paris at the Irish Cultural Centre is trying to reflect the issue. In Perspective, we spoke to the museum's director and one of the artists taking part.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>France student protests: What measures is the government taking?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:299d8311ed0a97f3b7f1e8a82e9742522a88380824a490e7b14833b24adeadf8</id><updated>2026-10-08T21:26:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:54:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-france-student-protests-what-measures-is-the-government-taking--c03d86896378.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261008-france-student-protests-what-measures-is-the-government-taking" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said in a televised address Wednesday evening that the country could not be "indifferent" to the concerns of protesting high school students, acknowledging that the "anger of young people does not come from nowhere". He denied that security forces have "orders to confront" the young people, and promised the government would present a plan to respond to the crisis at the end of October. But what measures could the French government introduce and will it be enough to calm the protests? France 24’s Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi takes a look.</summary></entry></feed>
